\begin_layout Standard
The coincidence between 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda^{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathfrak{H}}$
\end_inset

 and the order of 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{A}_{\mathfrak{H}}$
\end_inset

 in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Consistency-indices-for"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

 provides the raw indication of the extent to which (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:reciprocal-consistency-condition"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

) is satisfied.
 Except for the 
\begin_inset Formula $TA_{\text{opt}}$
\end_inset

 hierarchy model,
 the quantities coincide very closely.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Pant2022"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 reiterate the heuristic 
\begin_inset Formula $CR\apprle0.1$
\end_inset

 as a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

good-enough
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 condition for most purposes.
 All of the 
\begin_inset Formula $CR$
\end_inset

 values in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Consistency-indices-for"
plural "false"
